{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527805-info-on-the-warriors-of-glycon","id":1527805,"title":"Info on the Warriors of Glycon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-02T19:48:03-08:00","id":1527805,"title":"Info on the Warriors of Glycon","content":"Hello everyone,<br /> <br /> VDA20 introduced a new bloodline of the Followers of Set, the Warriors of Glycon (not to be confused with the yet-to-emerge Warrior Setites). I like it very much, but the only content on them I can find is what is in the core manual, in the clan appendix. Is there anything else on them elsewhere?<br /> For example, I would like to know more about their name. I have read Wikipedia's page on Glycon, which seems to be a snake deity whose cult began in modern day Turkey in mid-2nd century CE and didn't last very long. There were earlier snake cults both in the area and in Macedonia and elsewhere, of course, but the name &quot;Glycon&quot; seems tied to this cult in particular. Now, a Macedonian-Anatolian bloodline of snake-warriors makes total sense to me, especially considering that Echidna and Typhon are also linked to that geographical area in myths. However, mid-2nd century CE suggests a rather young bloodline, and the VDA20 manual states that they tend to be found in North Africa and are the current &quot;rulers&quot; of the clan - though not for long. This does not go well with the idea of them being such a young bloodline - Set himself disappeared in 33 BC or CE, so the bloodline would have emerged after his disappearance and somehow gained leadership of the clan in North Africa despite their name suggesting a Macedonian and Asia minor origin...<br /> <br /> Thanks to anyone who can help me find more material on them, or flesh them out a bit. So far I have a headcanon about Set travelling to Asia Minor, Macedonia and Greece after his infection by Apophis / Embrace and struggling there to control his Beast and his physical form, siring the Warriors of Glycon and Witches of Echidna in the process and giving rise to the many part-human-part-snake-related myths in the area. Later he returns to Egypt and sires the priest line. In this headcanon, Glycon and Echidna are two early infants of Set, and the cult of Glycon is not the origin of the bloodline's name, but a spilling of their name into Roman religion due to the actions of some clumsy member of the bloodline. &quot;Typhon&quot; is the combination of Set and his yet-to-be controlled Beast. I am aware of the theory on Typhon being a 2nd gen vampire diablerised by Set, or 3rd gen if Set was an infant of the Gangrel Antediluvian, and I am not rejecting it in principle. It would make sense for a Gangrel to have a Beast that makes him assume a combination of animal features, as Typhon was described like in myth. I just haven't figured out how exactly i want to interpret these ideas in my headcanon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T00:23:55-08:00","id":1527818,"title":"","content":"I strongly suspect the name might also be a referential nod to <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Glycon\" target=\"_blank\">a character</a> among the leading figures of the setite Fire Court as presented in <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Giovanni_Chronicles_III:_The_Sun_Has_Set\" target=\"_blank\">Giovanni Chronicles III: The Sun Has Set</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T04:05:40-08:00","id":1527829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527805-info-on-the-warriors-of-glycon?p=1527818#post1527818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I strongly suspect the name might also be a referential nod to <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Glycon\" target=\"_blank\">a character</a> among the leading figures of the setite Fire Court as presented in <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Giovanni_Chronicles_III:_The_Sun_Has_Set\" target=\"_blank\">Giovanni Chronicles III: The Sun Has Set</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u0130s it the Egyptian 6th or 7th gen Warrior Setite called Glycon? The problem is that part of the NPGs have to be retconned or given more details for the two new Setite bloodlines to make sense. <br /> The Glycon \u0130 have in mind was born (as a mortal) in 1148 according to the wiki. Way to late to have any relevance to the history of the bloodline in 1244, the year around which VDA20 events revolve. <br /> Rather, figures like the Scorpion King, Seterpenre and the legendary Wepwawet (who might never have existed) are good candidates for a rewrite as Warriors of Glycon, unless we want to introduce wholly new Mathuselahs for these two bloodlines (totally doable and fine) whose names have been cancelled and forgotten by the Modern Nights, given the hunting down to extinction of both lines by the priestly line with the aid of their Warrior Setite (NOT Warriors of Glycon: different discipline set, different clan weakness, different history and role). There is something about Set's childer having been 13, 6 of which are still in torpor in Tannis, though, which needs to be accounted for. Plus the likelihood that Set had other older childer who were all destroyed before those 13.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T04:43:38-08:00","id":1527830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527805-info-on-the-warriors-of-glycon?p=1527829#post1527829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u0130s it the Egyptian 6th or 7th gen Warrior Setite called Glycon? The problem is that part of the NPGs have to be retconned or given more details for the two new Setite bloodlines to make sense.<br /> The Glycon \u0130 have in mind was born (as a mortal) in 1148 according to the wiki. Way to late to have any relevance to the history of the bloodline in 1244, the year around which VDA20 events revolve.</div> </div> </div> </div>Must admit i'm not terribly familiar with the bloodline's story to say anything on the subject - not to mention i learned long, long ago to treat DAV and VtM canons as parallel timelines &amp; realities, to be connected or not in a need-to/inspiration basis only, for the sake of my sanity as ST. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> All of that said, i guess it would make sense for Fire Court's Glycon - whose role in the book and backstory resonate quite strongly with devotion &amp; servitude to priests/wise elders than a disputed leadership, to actually NOT be part of the line but one of the first Warrior Setites and have adopted the name/title as a reminder or slap in the face of the DA bloodline or something along those lines.<br /> <br /> My spur-of-moment ramblings on the subject as i go, at least.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527805-info-on-the-warriors-of-glycon?p=1527829#post1527829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rather, figures like the Scorpion King, Seterpenre and the legendary Wepwawet (who might never have existed) are good candidates for a rewrite as Warriors of Glycon, unless we want to introduce wholly new Mathuselahs for these two bloodlines (totally doable and fine) whose names have been cancelled and forgotten by the Modern Nights, given the hunting down to extinction of both lines by the priestly line with the aid of their Warrior Setite (NOT Warriors of Glycon: different discipline set, different clan weakness, different history and role). There is something about Set's childer having been 13, 6 of which are still in torpor in Tannis, though, which needs to be accounted for. Plus the likelihood that Set had other older childer who were all destroyed before those 13.</div> </div> </div> </div>One might also ask oneself where Kemintiri - and Nefertiti from Berlin by Night - figure or not among those legendary 13....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-03-2024, 07:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T21:54:53-08:00","id":1527902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527805-info-on-the-warriors-of-glycon?p=1527830#post1527830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> One might also ask oneself where Kemintiri - and Nefertiti from Berlin by Night - figure or not among those legendary 13....</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely. It depends on how one chooses to run Set's story and the clan's origin, so it's very much up to the ST.<br /> <br /> Were the 13 all embraced after Set's defeat by Horus and the Osirian League and after Set exterminated his surviving childer and followers to cancel all evidence of his defeat? Or were some embraced before?<br /> <br /> Did Set indeed exterminate his first group of childer and followers?<br /> <br /> Were they really 13, or was that a symbolic number chosen by the Methuselahs who survived the fall of Tanis and Set's disappearance?<br /> <br /> Are disloyal childer of Set like Kementiri included in the count (like, they are still holy because his blood flows in them) or excluded?<br /> <br /> Etc.<br /> <br /> But the introduction of two new Setite bloodlines in Dark Ages (and the Witches of Echidna survive into the modern nights and are mentioned in V20 supplements) means the early history of the clan probably has to be partially rewritten, and the canonical V20 lore has to be regarded as what Setites younger than 700 years have been led to believe about the history of their clan. Especially because in VDA20 these two bloodlines are not presented as some rare and politically insignificant groups: the Warriors of Glycon were the clan's rulers; the Witches of Echidna were popular even outside of the clan, especially in Hellenistic times, as oracles and mystic priestesses, and the clan's magic comes from their line, even though they were quite liberal in teaching it to others, especially before their extinction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T01:00:04-08:00","id":1527914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527805-info-on-the-warriors-of-glycon?p=1527902#post1527902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Were they really 13,.</div> </div> </div> </div>Complicated<br /> Sutekh had 13 <b>known</b> Children<br /> <br /> Nakhthorheb- Libellus Sanguinis 3: Wolves at the Door<br /> Seterpenre - Libellus Sanguinis 3: Wolves at the Door<br /> Maatkare - Libellus Sanguinis 3: Wolves at the Door<br /> Wepwawet - Clanbook: Followers of Set Revised<br /> The Scorpion King - Cairo by Night<br /> Nebmaatsutekh - Player's Guide to the Low Clans<br /> Kemintiri - The Kindred Most Wanted<br /> Nefertiti - Berlin by Night<br /> Nephthys - Rage Across Egypt<br /> Qufur am-Heru the First - Children of the Night<br /> Sobek - Chaining the Beast / Mummy 2nd ed<br /> Ta-urt - Nights of Prophecy<br /> Wadjet - Mummy 2nd ed<br /> <br /> Obviously Nephthys never was a Hierophants however and Wadjet's actions are recorded in the Isis Fragments and remembered by the Children of Osiris, but she has been stricken from the history of the Followers of Set, so she is out too<br /> The Scorpion King He fell victim to the Week of the Midnight Sun in 3100 BC.<br /> Kemintiri is called &quot;the rogue hierophant, traitor to Set&quot; - but the Clan wants her back for her knowledge of the Spell of Life and after all, she is the Children of Set AND a de-facto Hierophant and an Eternal of Sothis<br /> <br /> We have a few Hierophants known by name but not the dircet children of Sutekh<br /> ...or at least not stated to be one, except Shemti's case, he is stated not to be one of the original thirteen, but the Hierophant of Faiyum<br /> The childer of Set that is worshipped in Faiyum is Sobek (Clanbook: Revised, p.47). Since the stewardship over a founding temple is (according to the example we see in El Kharga, in Nights of Prophecy, p.26) passed along the line of succession, it is likely that Shemti is a childe of Sobek than to be a direct childe of Set.<br /> <br /> Shemti was the Hierophant of Faiyum as of 1795 (Clanbook: Followers of Set Revised)<br /> Tenermentu was the Hierophant of Siwa during the Dark Ages (Libellus Sanguinis 3: Wolves at the Door)<br /> The First Cantor of Thebes, the Hierophant of Thebes in 1205 (Dark Ages Clan Novel 4: Setite)<br /> <br /> But it is worth to mention, 3 Children was out, and we know 3 other Follow of Set<br /> The 13 basically stayed <br /> <br /> But since you don't have to be the direct Children of Sutekh, just have to be an Eternal of Sothis to be a Hierophant?<br /> Anything is possible, including but not limited to the fact, a direct children of Sutekh, tho' it is a descendant of the God of Storms himself and an Eternal of Sothis not necessarily have to be a Hierophant<br /> But possibly expected to be one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}